        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The base rate/reference class is the last 13 official headline CPI annual inflation prints. Their mean is 2.59 percent, their median is 2.12 percent, but the post-April energy-regime sample is materially higher: April-August prints are 4.01, 4.08, 3.40, 3.56, and 3.97 percent. I therefore put more weight on near-term persistence than on the full-sample mean."
